# Strings of the Zig bk-* tools (bk-pak, bk-image, bk-table, bk-video): en.
# Format as the editor kit's tables (see tools/zig/bk_l10n.zig). Keep {0}..{9}, <placeholders>,
# option and command names as in en.lang. The usage: and <tool>: prefixes are not here: they stay English.

tool.usage.lang=--lang <code>  shows help and messages in another language ({0}).\nWithout it, BK_LANG and then the operating system's language decide.
pak.usage.body=pack    writes every file under <dir> as a stored (uncompressed) entry,\n        sorted, with / separators: the format the game mounts and the\n        release packager writes. Same tree, same bytes.\nunpack  extracts stored and deflate entries into <dir> after checking the\n        whole archive; nothing is written if any entry is unsafe or damaged.\nlist    prints size, method and archive name of every entry.\nverify  checks every entry's name, CRC-32 and size.
pak.usage.note=An existing output file is only replaced with --force. Zip64 archives\n(more than 65,535 entries or 4 GiB) are not supported.
