sprite.usage.compose=compose     packs the frames a sprite-sequence description names into\n            <out-name>.tga and describes the animations in <out-name>.san,\n            as spcomp did
sprite.usage.desc=<desc-dir> holds anims.txt, one [section] per animation:\n  dirs=<n>                 number of directions (required)\n  dir<k> seq=<i>,<j>,...   frame indices of direction k (required)\n  frametime=<ms>           one frame's show time (default 125)\n  speed=<f>                translation speed (default 0)\n  cycled=<0|1>             cycled or one-shot (default 1)\n  shift=<x>,<y>            every frame's shift (default 0,0)\n  dir<k> shift=<x>,<y>     direction k's frames' shift (default: shift)\n  frame<i> shift=<x>,<y>   frame i's shift (default: its direction's)\nFrame i of animation <name> is <desc-dir>/<name>/<iii>.tga; an animation\nnamed default has the one frame <desc-dir>/1.tga. The section names are\nthe animation slots (idle, run, death, ...; default and effect are idle).
sprite.usage.options=--force     replace <out-name>.tga and .san when they are already there\n--modules   where the engine's StreamIO and Image libraries are (default:\n            beside bk-sprite, then ../lib, then ..)
