font.usage.intro=Renders characters 32..255 of the charset's code page (or the characters of\n--chars, --set and --clusters) into <dir>/1.tga and\ndescribes them (metrics, texture rects, A/B/C spacing, kerning) in\n<dir>/1.tfd, as FontGen did, plus <dir>/1_h.dds, the texture the game\nreads: a font directory the game loads like Data/Fonts/small.
font.usage.options=--ttf        a .ttf/.otf/.ttc file, or a face name looked up in the system\n             font folders (best effort; a file is the reliable way)\n--height     cell height in pixels, ascent + descent (default 20)\n--weight     400 regular (default); 600 or more picks the bold face of a\n             name, or emboldens a face that is not bold\n--italic     picks the italic face of a name, or slants one that is not\n--no-aa      every pixel fully on or off\n--charset    ansi or default (code page 1252, default), easteurope (1250),\n             russian (1251), or the code page number\n--chars      a UTF-8 file: every distinct BMP character in it, plus ASCII\n             32..126 (Unicode mode; characters the face lacks are left out)\n--set        latin1, cyrillic or devanagari: a built-in character range (Unicode\n             mode; repeatable, and adds to --chars)\n--clusters   the cluster table the language-mods export wrote (U+E000<TAB>cluster\n             lines): every cluster becomes one glyph under its Private Use Area\n             character, shaped with this --ttf (Unicode mode)\n--script     the ISO 15924 tag the clusters are shaped with (default Deva)\n--language   the BCP 47 tag the clusters are shaped with (default hi)\n--fallback-ttf\n             a second .ttf/.otf file for the characters the --ttf face lacks,\n             drawn at the same height on its baseline (Unicode mode)\n--base       the folder of a game font (1.tfd, 1_h.dds) to keep as it is: its\n             characters stay, and only the requested ones it lacks are added\n--face-index the face inside a .ttc collection (default 0)\n--out        output directory, created if missing (default .)\n--force      replace an existing font in <dir>\n--modules    where the engine's StreamIO and Image libraries are (default:\n             beside bk-font, then ../lib)
