map.usage.commands=to-bzm      converts a map from .xml to the game's binary .bzm\nto-xml      converts a map from .bzm to .xml\nminimap     draws a map's minimap as <map>_c.dds, <map>_l.dds and <map>_h.dds,\n            <px> square, with the object database and tilesets of --data\nobj2mod     builds a .mod from the Blender exporter's OBJ and its optional\n            skeleton and animation files (tools/blender)\nvalidate-obj2mod  checks those files the way obj2mod does, writing nothing
map.usage.directory=A directory is searched recursively (to-bzm takes its .xml files, to-xml its\n.bzm files, minimap both, the newer of the two when a map has both, as the\ngame reads it) and the tree is mirrored under --out.
map.usage.options=--out       output directory (default: beside each input)\n--force     replace outputs that are already there\n--data      the game's Data directory (default ./Data): a map names road and\n            river descriptions, a minimap also needs objects and tilesets\n--modules   where the engine's StreamIO and Image libraries are (default:\n            beside bk-map, then ../lib, then ..)
